<%# Generic answer fragment — renders the §4 envelope's `result` Hash for any
    calculator that has no bespoke result view yet (and for the test double). Each
    key/value becomes a hero-result row: humanized key as the eyebrow, the value as
    a big tabular-nums number (DESIGN.md §4). Keeps the seam honest — the page works
    for a calculator the moment its math + page exist, before custom result copy.

    Locals: calc. %>
<div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
  <div class="border-l-[5px] border-primary p-8">
    <% calc.result.each do |key, value| %>
      <div class="not-first:mt-6 not-first:border-t not-first:border-rule not-first:pt-6">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent"><%= key.to_s.humanize %></p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink"><%= percentage_display(value) %></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
